# Used by `npm run dns:apply` only.
#
# Nothing in this file reaches the Worker. Verified: wrangler ignores .env for
# both `dev` and `deploy`. Worker config lives in wrangler.jsonc, Worker
# secrets in .dev.vars locally and `wrangler secret put` in production.
#
# Note the name. Do NOT call this CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: wrangler auto-loads
# .env and uses that variable for its own auth, so a DNS-scoped token under
# that name replaces your OAuth session and breaks every wrangler command
# with a misleading "Failed to automatically retrieve account IDs" error.
#
# Create the token at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
#   Permissions:    Zone > DNS > Edit
#   Zone Resources: Include > Specific zone > ragedb.io
#
# Scope it to the single zone. Not the Global API Key — that carries every
# permission on the account and cannot be revoked independently of your login.
CLOUDFLARE_DNS_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. The script resolves the zone id itself, falling back to your
# wrangler login for the lookup, so set this only if that fails.
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
